h":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1vy.1--plan/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-28T08:53:53.604862+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-1vy.1--plan","local_name":"sase-1vy.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-1vy","agent_clan_generation":"20261128031554","agent_session":"sase-1vy.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"sase-1vy.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1vy[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Backlog Epic 2: leak gate, federation freshness, bench integrity, [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]and load flakes (final round)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The five most important remaining open task beads are fixed and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]closed. The land agent verifies, closes this final epic, and stops:[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the user capped the backlog chain at two rounds, so no Backlog Epic[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]3 is planned.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]backlog_epic_2.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/backlog_epic_2.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1vy[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1vy/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the leak-detector thread poison on the CI Telemetry gate [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1vg)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]leak-gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]leak-gate: fix the root cause of sase-1vg. Read sase-1vg and all of its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes first. ACE pilot tests intermittently leave a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-config-token-refresh thread alive past the leak-detector snapshot, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]poisoning global sase.config.core._live_config_token_refresh_threads on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the CI Telemetry test-cost gate (run 46071761552: 63,676 passed in 2:03 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inside the 180m cap, failing only this gate). Roughly 1 in 3 recent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Telemetry runs. Fix it at its root; do not exempt the name from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]detector. Verify with the cost lane and just check through sase tool run[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check, then close sase-1vg and the phase bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Federation cache-only reads must not report stale snapshots as[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]ok (sase-1aw)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]federation-freshness[dim] · [dim][/dim]after leak-gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]federation-freshness: fix sase-1aw. Read sase-1aw and all of its notes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]first. Cache-only federation reads ignore the last network failure and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]label the stale cache ok; the bug body carries the reproduction and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proposed fix. Make cache-only reads surface the failure instead of a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stale ok. Add or update a regression test for the stale-after-failure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shape. Run sase tool run check, then close sase-1aw and the phase bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Axe j/k benchmark must not capture Agents-tab samples under [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]load (sase-199)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]bench-integrity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after federation-freshness[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bench-integrity: fix sase-199. Read sase-199 and all of its notes first.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]The Axe j/k bench collects samples from tabs other than the measured one[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]under load (4 corroborations). Scope the sample window to the measured [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tab so bench results stay meaningful. Cover with a regression test that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fails on the old cross-tab capture. Run sase tool run check, then close [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-199 and the phase bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stale index-lock recovery flake under loaded scoped check [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1kr)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]index-lock-flake[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bench-integrity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]index-lock-flake: fix sase-1kr. Read sase-1kr and all of its notes first[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](7 corroborations; pairs with sase-1s4, a test that leaves a stale lock [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in a real checkout). Make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]test_run_workspace_git_command_recovers_stale_index_lock robust under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the loaded scoped lane, or fix the product recovery path it guards if [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the flake exposes a real race. Do not close on a single green rerun; [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]show the node green across repeated loaded runs. Run sase tool run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check, then close sase-1kr and the phase bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Tool-admission overlap flake: rule out a real limit violation [bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1vw)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]admission-overlap-flake[dim] · [dim][/dim]after index-lock-flake[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]admission-overlap-flake: fix sase-1vw. Read sase-1vw and all of its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes first (related sase-1ve tracks a different node in the same [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]module). test_limit_two_with_four_runs_never_overlaps_more_than_two [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failed once under host load with no admission change in the finding [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diff, then passed 5/5 isolated plus a green whole-module run. Determine [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whether the overlap measurement needs a semantic wait or the failure is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a real admission-limit violation with more than two concurrent runs at [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]limit two; fix whichever it is. Do not close on a single green rerun. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Run sase tool run check, then close sase-1vw and the phase bead.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1vy","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-astra","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1vy.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-1vy.1"},"source_run_id":"run-43f6dc47be8b48feba31ea592807f57a","started_at":"2026-11-28T08:16:36.531179+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"0689c8e465c559fb6e9a1c78ed1f3317df97131dfbe5e2815d50ad3b1d0c8605","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1vy.3--1/chat.md","size_bytes":8783},"commits":{"digest":"85d54c80f2c6462128ce411217719bdfe76c5f9dbef35222a05503da6b17bfe1","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1vy.3--1/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"0e2e9d635b6be09d75667f54cabe7c9af2d977aaf8d46609d9d5c40b23f6faa9","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1vy.3--1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":65},"meta":{"digest":"59b1c9724636ae220c18bb04954584715c7ec53600d1aa84a001379947773292","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1vy.3--1/meta.json","size_bytes":651},"prompt":{"digest":"e05ff90ad466b7d894b18a10da0aa0e7dc7d054c7c7b0e9af56e369e12c71662","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1vy